WEBVTT

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:12.700
Three, three, three.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.700
Just got a wire that says you got a fugitive on board, Fred.

00:01:37.996 --> 00:01:39.656
Guess we'll have to give you a train to what's over.

00:01:39.816 --> 00:01:41.116
All right, Sheriff. Go ahead.

00:01:41.356 --> 00:01:41.916
Who is it?

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.480
His name was John Brant.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:44.980
Then up for murder and got away.

00:01:45.676 --> 00:01:48.656
Bryant, eh? Oh, yeah. Read about him in the paper.

00:01:49.164 --> 00:01:50.284
Well, I hope you get in, Cheryl.

00:02:30.348 --> 00:02:30.528
Go.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.500
If we don't know this country very well, we'll go round the hill and head him off.

00:05:29.084 --> 00:05:29.584
any place.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:50.520
that

00:06:29.628 --> 00:06:29.988
So good.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.600
some of the boys and drag the lake.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:22.670
well i guess you got me come on out stranger i ain't so long you're a pretty smart hombre

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:28.320
and you've got plenty of nerve strikes me the boss could use somebody like you what's your name

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:37.640
Smith, ain't it? That's the handle most of you fast travelers use. Ah, that's as good as any.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:44.920
Mine's Jones. Say, you're pretty near all in, ain't you? Better come on.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.280
up with me to the hideout and meet the big chief we're short a couple of hands

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.590
I'm bringing a new man in to see the chief.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.730
Dick, I'd like for you to know my friend, Mr.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:41.950
Wait a minute, don't tell me.

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:42.750
Let me guess.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.130
Name's Smith, ain't it?

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:46.130
That's right.

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:34.500
Yeah, but if we ever do get in a tight spot, this tunnel runs clear back through the mountains, so we almost have a getaway.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:37.460
You wait here a minute.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:57.160
Well, as long as you brought him in, we've got to do something with him.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.580
Say, we need a new cook.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:10.030
The last one got hurt bad yesterday.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.200
Come here, come in and clean up this mess.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:45.630
And if I deal, deal me in.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:46.310
Me too.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:47.880
Nothing like me, boys.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.320
I saw where that one came from, Chief.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:17.170
Your eyes is kind of going back on you, ain't they, Jones?

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:18.790
Oh, no, they aren't.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.300
I got it!

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:09.660
You better keep that dude to mind his own business or we'll be needing another cook.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:44.550
$1,000 reward will be paid for information leading to the capture of John Brandt, sentenced to the Maryland state prison when he was found with a body of George Wagner, wealthy club man in the Loveness apartment of Mrs. Joseph Conlon.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:57.960
Brandt escaped from prison May 14th and is thought to have headed west. You know, that's the bird we lost at the lake yesterday. I'll have to send in a report on him.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.030
Funny thing about that case, the husband of the wound that was mixed up in it,

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:06.870
flows around these parts too.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:10.240
I got a handbill on him just yesterday.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:15.770
He might have saved Brandt if he'd only turned up and testified.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:18.720
At least lie, that's what Brandt said at the trial.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:29.940
I wonder what would have happened if...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.380
Brandt ever ran across Conlon.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.050
I'll bet he would've made it plenty hot for him.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:48.560
You sure made that plenty hot for me.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:54.330
Mighty fine of you to mix in that fight last night.

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:57.480
Wasn't any of your battle, and I won't forget it.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:58.750
I won't either.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.320
Smith, you get down to the trail and water the horses.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:06.700
Thought I was supposed to cook.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.030
Get going.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:15.210
Wait a minute, Jones.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:16.570
I want to talk to you.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.120
Just who is this fellow you call Smith?

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:20.430
What do you know about him?

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:24.670
Well, I know his name ain't Smith, but he's got plenty of nerve,

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:26.550
and we could use a little of that around here.

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:29.380
Besides, I know a square guy when I see one.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:29.910
Yeah.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:35.990
he might be a star packer some of them are square guys so you're worried about

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:39.820
him huh well I'll show you he's all right you know that safe job down at

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:43.060
Sagebrush we were talking about well Smith and I'll pull out ourselves just

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:46.710
the two of us a star packer wouldn't do that would he all right pick him up

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:52.340
down at the trail at noon and if you get in a jam hideout down at Blind Pete's

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:52.950
all right

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:18.670
the law won't write in on us. Chance. They're all out looking for rusters.

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.790
Were you gentlemen interested in looking at something?

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:36.410
I'll say so.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.430
Have you any, uh, rutabaga?

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:39.560
Why, certainly.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.400
I almost forgot what we came here for.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:14.920
time to the

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:24.160
next mail get in? At three o'clock. Will it be on time? It never misses.

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:32.200
Wouldn't you like one of these hat bands?

00:16:32.556 --> 00:16:33.216
Bye, yeah.

00:16:34.764 --> 00:16:36.704
No, I guess that'll be all.

00:16:37.164 --> 00:16:39.164
Won't there be anything else?

00:16:39.628 --> 00:16:39.888
No.

00:16:41.708 --> 00:16:43.588
Well, maybe my friend here would like something.

00:16:44.108 --> 00:16:44.948
What will you have?

00:16:47.724 --> 00:16:48.724
Why?

00:16:49.612 --> 00:16:50.492
I'll take the same.

00:17:03.356 --> 00:17:03.856
Hey.

00:17:17.468 --> 00:17:18.348
Be careful with them.

00:17:20.444 --> 00:17:22.444
Are you sure you wouldn't cast one of these hat bands?

00:17:22.716 --> 00:17:23.716
It's special.

00:17:23.716 --> 00:17:24.716
Yeah.

00:17:26.364 --> 00:17:27.404
I'll get one next time.

00:17:27.964 --> 00:17:29.224
That will be $10 each.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.540
My friend will pay for it.

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:54.670
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:04.240
I suppose you want more liniment for that rheumatism of yours.

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:06.520
Well, how'd you guess it, Miss Sally?

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:08.080
If you're limping like that...

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:08.240
Oh!

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.850
Wait, I think I gave you the wrong bottle.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:25.500
Yeah?

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:34.160
no this is the right one i don't know what's the matter with me today

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:59.830
look dad leave a couple of men in your store with the lights on

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.720
Your safe will be robbed tonight.

00:19:03.292 --> 00:19:05.912
Do you think those fellows who were just here had anything to do with this?

00:19:06.684 --> 00:19:08.584
Why, no, they couldn't have written it.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:09.520
Bye.

00:19:09.724 --> 00:19:11.364
I was talking to one of them all the time.

00:19:12.092 --> 00:19:13.452
I'd better tell the sheriff.

00:19:15.292 --> 00:19:17.332
We'll be waiting for him, all right.

00:19:18.684 --> 00:19:20.464
but without any lights on.

00:19:42.668 --> 00:19:43.528
No light, Jay.

00:19:44.652 --> 00:19:45.412
That's bad.

00:19:46.412 --> 00:19:47.412
One try.

00:19:47.596 --> 00:19:47.936
Nothing.

00:19:49.804 --> 00:19:50.564
Better than me go.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:28.910
behind you get out don't wait for me come on you're all right you can hide out at blind pete

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:29.970
and there won't be no time before you're

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:46.710
That guy looked mighty familiar to me. I wonder if it could have been...

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:46.950
What's that, Sheriff?

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.990
Oh, never mind. Nobody's trying to tail him in the dark, anyhow.

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:47.510
What's the dope piece?

00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:54.350
The three o'clock stage is carrying the mine payroll.

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:58.070
That's all Walsh wanted to know.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.180
How's Smith?

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:17.850
We gonna hard hold him.

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:18.930
What is he?

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:20.900
He's in there.

00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:34.160
Come in.

00:22:34.340 --> 00:22:38.020
How are you, partner?

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:39.440
Oh, I'm feeling great.

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:42.260
And I'll sure be glad to get out of this place.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:01.900
You better wait a while yet, partner.

00:23:02.830 --> 00:23:04.270
We've got a tough job to do.

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:07.690
We're sticking up to three o'clock stage, down by the bend.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.500
And it ain't no place for invalids.

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:14.860
I'm glad to see you're coming along, all right.

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:18.470
Well, so long, I'll be seeing you.

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:26.560
Down by the bend.

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:29.780
Yes.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.740
You'll be seen.

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:57.370
A few minutes, boys, so get ready.

00:25:33.930 --> 00:25:36.430
Good agents haven't been very active lately, haven't they?

00:25:36.670 --> 00:25:37.810
Well, we've got them scared.

00:25:39.470 --> 00:25:41.640
Get rid of that gun, and don't turn around.

00:25:42.700 --> 00:25:43.880
I'll throw off that money box.

00:25:50.100 --> 00:25:52.360
Keep driving straight ahead, and don't look back.

00:26:07.870 --> 00:26:09.250
This ought to be a good haul.

00:26:14.330 --> 00:26:15.250
Here he comes now.

00:26:45.450 --> 00:26:47.090
I tell you, he came up behind us.

00:26:47.270 --> 00:26:48.810
We didn't even get a look at him.

00:26:49.430 --> 00:26:50.630
He must be telling the truth, Chief.

00:26:50.870 --> 00:26:51.990
There ain't a sign on the box anywhere.

00:26:53.210 --> 00:26:54.250
All right, get going.

00:26:54.490 --> 00:26:54.870
Get it.

00:27:00.990 --> 00:27:02.130
Somebody's pulled a pass.

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:06.900
Say, did you tell Smith about this?

00:27:07.700 --> 00:27:08.080
No.

00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:10.940
Besides, he couldn't have done it anyway.

00:27:11.340 --> 00:27:12.340
He's dark blind Pete.

00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:13.300
Yeah.

00:27:14.820 --> 00:27:15.780
Well, getting out of it, boys.

00:27:16.320 --> 00:27:20.380
We'll split up and see if we can't find this word that has such taken ways of mine payroll.

00:27:30.160 --> 00:27:30.380
I'm ready.

00:28:04.284 --> 00:28:06.064
Quick, Sally, come out here. It's important.

00:28:31.310 --> 00:28:43.070
He could have saved me if he'd have wanted, but he let me go to jail.

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:46.260
Well, someday I'll meet him.

00:28:46.360 --> 00:28:48.220
When I do...

00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:52.760
I'm sorry, but why do you have to associate with that gang?

00:28:53.230 --> 00:28:56.090
That's just the kind of a place I'll find the man I'm looking for.

00:28:56.860 --> 00:28:59.830
And besides, I got a pal that doesn't belong there.

00:29:01.468 --> 00:29:02.788
Well, I guess I better be riding.

00:29:03.644 --> 00:29:06.244
Now, don't forget in the hollow of a tree down by the forks.

00:29:06.652 --> 00:29:08.332
Oh, you call the sheriff, you got another note.

00:29:09.500 --> 00:29:10.760
Oh, you've lost your hat band.

00:29:11.292 --> 00:29:12.772
Wait, I'll get you another from the store.

00:29:27.516 --> 00:29:28.516
What are you?

00:29:29.468 --> 00:29:29.768
All right.

00:29:51.770 --> 00:29:57.510
didn't expect to see you here partner how'd the state's job come wrong why not

00:29:57.510 --> 00:29:59.420
so good somebody beat us to it

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:01.840
Fact is, the boys kind of think you did it.

00:30:02.364 --> 00:30:03.784
Looks funny, too, you being away.

00:30:04.316 --> 00:30:06.936
I'd sort of suspect you myself if it hadn't been for the way the other night.

00:30:07.164 --> 00:30:09.244
Well, maybe I did rob the stage.

00:30:11.644 --> 00:30:13.404
Say, just where were you anyway?

00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:16.040
You haven't been over to see Sally, have you?

00:30:17.212 --> 00:30:18.532
You know, we're pals and all that.

00:30:19.068 --> 00:30:20.088
I like you fine, Smith.

00:30:20.604 --> 00:30:22.504
But if I thought you were cutting in on Sally,

00:30:23.068 --> 00:30:25.068
You don't think you're good enough for her, do you?

00:30:26.140 --> 00:30:27.040
Do you think you are?

00:30:28.220 --> 00:30:28.720
No.

00:30:29.756 --> 00:30:29.996
All right.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.000
I don't.

00:30:31.724 --> 00:30:32.524
Maybe you're right.

00:30:33.516 --> 00:30:35.756
I might have been though if a woman hadn't double-crossed me.

00:30:36.972 --> 00:30:38.012
It was several years ago.

00:30:38.860 --> 00:30:40.060
I came out here from Baltimore.

00:30:43.020 --> 00:30:44.020
Baltimore?

00:30:44.652 --> 00:30:44.992
Yeah.

00:30:45.168 --> 00:30:45.668
Why?

00:30:46.476 --> 00:30:48.616
I knew somebody in Baltimore once.

00:30:50.636 --> 00:30:52.356
I came out here to regain my health.

00:30:53.292 --> 00:30:54.132
When I went back,

00:30:54.636 --> 00:30:56.736
I found my wife in the arms of another man.

00:30:57.484 --> 00:30:58.084
We fought.

00:30:58.604 --> 00:30:59.804
And I killed him, Smith.

00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:03.780
I got away and headed out here.

00:31:05.116 --> 00:31:06.436
I've been a fugitive ever since.

00:31:07.452 --> 00:31:08.652
What is her name, Conlon?

00:31:11.196 --> 00:31:12.196
What do you want to know for?

00:31:12.540 --> 00:31:14.360
I think I read about it in the paper.

00:31:15.804 --> 00:31:16.804
Yeah.

00:31:17.308 --> 00:31:18.708
I suppose it was in all the papers.

00:31:20.412 --> 00:31:22.012
Funny, I never saw one after I left.

00:31:27.196 --> 00:31:29.056
And you never knew what happened after that?

00:31:29.596 --> 00:31:29.856
No.

00:31:31.500 --> 00:31:33.160
I never heard any more about it.

00:31:38.444 --> 00:31:39.924
Come on, you need a drink, partner.

00:31:44.556 --> 00:31:46.316
You know we ought to give up this racket, though.

00:31:47.660 --> 00:31:50.160
Gonna lead his boat to a rope necktie one of these days.

00:32:01.470 --> 00:32:02.070
Hi, boys.

00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:05.420
Here's a note I picked up down at Blind Pete.

00:32:11.550 --> 00:32:13.650
Well, boys, we've struck it rich.

00:32:14.280 --> 00:32:17.300
The mine's shipping out a load of gold bullion on the afternoon stage.

00:32:18.540 --> 00:32:18.920
Tomorrow.

00:32:19.630 --> 00:32:21.490
I'm going to retire after this haul.

00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:24.880
Not a chance of Walt winning all back at cards.

00:32:25.210 --> 00:32:26.410
Well, my working days are over.

00:32:26.530 --> 00:32:27.470
Well, do what's that?

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:34.180
afraid of that guy oh he's all right ever since he's been here somebody's been

00:32:34.180 --> 00:32:38.470
tipping off the sheriff I think he's a stool pigeon he's got the wrong dope on

00:32:38.470 --> 00:32:39.710
that bullion shipment though

00:33:50.260 --> 00:33:52.200
What are you getting all slicked up for?

00:33:52.620 --> 00:33:54.180
Oh, I'm just going shopping.

00:33:54.590 --> 00:33:55.820
Shopping? For what?

00:33:56.220 --> 00:33:59.890
Here, hold this. I'm going shopping.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:05.120
for for eggs you know if I don't have eggs in the morning the boys will be

00:34:05.120 --> 00:34:29.900
squawking so long if I'm beginning to think maybe

00:34:31.260 --> 00:34:35.010
Well, sure took you a long time to get wise to yourself, didn't it?

00:34:35.530 --> 00:34:38.990
He's going down now to tell them about the bullion job, which ain't tomorrow.

00:34:40.570 --> 00:34:42.450
We're gonna bring that stage up here this afternoon.

00:34:43.240 --> 00:34:44.940
The stuff's too heavy to move a horse back.

00:34:45.450 --> 00:34:49.150
I'll follow him and find out. If we come back together, he's all right.

00:34:49.670 --> 00:34:51.030
But if I send him back alone...

00:34:51.630 --> 00:34:52.650
We know what to do.

00:35:22.460 --> 00:35:24.340
I believe that fellow Brad is still alive.

00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:28.160
It's going to be like it is him at the door the night of the storeholder.

00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:31.810
Must have gotten out of that lake somehow.

00:35:33.330 --> 00:35:35.830
I believe we better take these handbills over and talk to Sally.

00:36:37.930 --> 00:36:41.740
Say, buddy, take this to Miss Sally, will you?

00:36:42.080 --> 00:36:42.400
Sure.

00:36:42.660 --> 00:36:44.060
And see that she gets it personally.

00:36:45.220 --> 00:36:45.640
Thanks.

00:37:00.444 --> 00:37:00.784
Sally.

00:37:01.596 --> 00:37:03.636
Man outside told me to give this to you.

00:37:04.128 --> 00:37:04.628
Thank you.

00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:25.700
Did you want something, Sheriff?

00:37:25.952 --> 00:37:26.892
Well, yes, Miss Sally.

00:37:27.580 --> 00:37:29.540
I wanted you to identify a couple of men for me.

00:37:30.028 --> 00:37:32.468
Were these the two men were in the store the day of the holdup?

00:37:40.588 --> 00:37:41.888
I think these are the men, Sheriff.

00:37:44.716 --> 00:37:46.716
I don't believe I can recognize them.

00:37:48.076 --> 00:37:49.236
Well, maybe we're wrong.

00:37:50.444 --> 00:37:51.204
Thanks, Miss Sally.

00:37:58.732 --> 00:37:59.992
Sally, since you're so hot.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.500
Bye-bye.

00:38:01.276 --> 00:38:02.156
Kind of hard to believe.

00:38:03.004 --> 00:38:04.544
She knows more than she's telling us.

00:38:04.988 --> 00:38:06.048
Maybe we ought to trailer.

00:39:09.596 --> 00:39:10.416
Hello, Joan.

00:39:11.164 --> 00:39:12.264
Where'd you come from?

00:39:13.244 --> 00:39:15.644
I just came in to help you carry back them eggs.

00:39:16.668 --> 00:39:18.168
Hey, what's eatin' you?

00:39:18.332 --> 00:39:19.692
You aren't acting yourself.

00:39:21.756 --> 00:39:22.256
Oh.

00:39:22.396 --> 00:39:22.896
Nothing.

00:39:23.868 --> 00:39:24.648
I guess I need a drink.

00:39:27.516 --> 00:39:28.076
Picks me a drink.

00:39:53.100 --> 00:39:54.860
You've got to get out of here. The sheriff is after you.

00:39:55.212 --> 00:39:57.192
He acted funny when I told him about the stage holdup.

00:39:57.372 --> 00:39:59.492
And today he came in and showed me your picture on reward notice.

00:40:00.090 --> 00:40:04.560
